class_name LevelMaps
## Grey-box test levels as text. One character is one 32 pixel tile.
##   #  solid block       P  player start      D  dog start
##   ?  something the dog is curious about
##   !  something the dog is wary of
##   >  level exit
##   E  an enemy (a bramble)
##   =  a gold plate          |  a gold gate, open while a gold plate is pressed
##   -  a blue plate          :  a blue gate
##   _  a heavy blue plate that only the player can press
##   ~  a plank that holds the dog and breaks under the player
##   +  a sandwich to throw   S  a squirrel that bolts right (Z bolts left)
##   $  a key                 &  a locked door that a key opens
##   *  a treat to pick up    %  food that tempts a hungry dog
## "puzzle": true makes it a puzzle room: a fall restarts it, and the dog cannot
## bound to you. "hunger" sets how hungry the dog starts (0 to 1), and "skills"
## sets what it already knows, e.g. {"stay": 2}.
##   a-z  a text label, defined in "labels"
## "theme" picks the scenery: woods, meadow, town or night.
## The player jumps 3.5 tiles high and about 5 tiles far at full speed.

